    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Agram is one of the most popular card games in Niger. Another version is played in northern Mali (Gao, Timbuktu, Kidal) and has spread to Cameroon as Fapfap. It is related to Spar or Sipa in Ghana and West Africa, probably descended from a European game introduced during the slave trade era.',
      originCountries: [
        'Niger',
        'Mali',
      ],
      timeline: [
        'Documented in modern card-game surveys as a popular Niger game.',
        'Related local forms such as Sink-Sink and Fapfap use similar last-trick structure.',
      ],
      evolution: 'Regional variants mostly change hand size and scoring stakes, while keeping the last-trick objective.',
      cultural: 'Known for tactical card conservation because only the final trick matters.',
    },
